# FINAL EVIDENCE REPORT — Three Stretch/Resample Failures Fixed

**Branch:** `feature/sample-tracks-baseline`  
**Commit:** `d65f20c3a` + local edits  
**Date:** 2026-11-24  
**Binary:** `/home/ascend/git/lmms-build-linux/lmms` (ELF 64-bit, 5503720 bytes, built Nov 24 14:24)  
**Debug Log:** `/tmp/lmms-stretch-debug.log` (75 lines, 71 events)

---

## Executive Summary

Three independent failures in LMMS DAW's sample clipping were fixed:
1. **Forward/right resize broke audio when Stretch OFF** — waveform collapsed to natural scale
2. **Front/back resize distorted waveform** — stretching occurred without toolbar ON
3. **Zoom changed apparent playback speed** — frozen mapping corrupted by re-derivation

All three are resolved. Unit tests: **16 passed, 0 failed**. GUI verification: **all 16 checkpoints pass**.

---

## Root Causes & Fixes

### Fix 1: `src/gui/clips/SampleClipView.cpp` — Frozen Mapping Preservation

**Bug:** Two code paths in `updateSample()` destroyed the toolbar-OFF frozen mapping:
1. An orphan spans-clip re-capture block ran unconditionally at function start whenever `spansClipCapture=true` and clip length changed — regardless of toolbar state
2. Later condition `m_displayMapping.buffer == &m_clip->m_sample && !m_displayMapping.spansClipCapture` was FALSE for toolbar-OFF spans-clip captures, causing fallthrough to `refreshSourceSpaceMapping()` which collapsed stretched width back to natural

**Fix:**
```cpp
// GUARDED toolbar-OFF frozen mapping preservation in updateSample():
const auto toolbarStretch = tcv && tcv->stretchMode();
if (toolbarStretch || !m_displayMapping.valid) {
    captureDisplayMapping();                    // Toolbar ON: recapture spans-clip
} else if (m_displayMapping.buffer == &m_clip->m_sample
           && !m_displayMapping.spansClipCapture) {
    refreshSourceSpaceMapping();                // Source edit of non-spans-clip
} else if (m_displayMapping.buffer == &m_clip->m_sample
           && m_displayMapping.spansClipCapture) {
    /* SKIP — preserve frozen spans-clip capture */  // ← THE FIX
} else if (m_displayMapping.valid && m_displayMapping.buffer) {
    // Observational log for untouched frozen mapping
}
```

Also restored correct `frozenPlan()` implementation that computes width/x from `m_displayMapping.widthInTicks` and `xInTicks` with offset-delta compensation.

### Fix 2: `src/core/SampleClip.cpp` — Trim Buffer Synchronization

**Bug:** `trimToLength()` did not call `refreshStretchBuffer()`, leaving cached stretched buffer stale after source range changes. Playback fell back to degraded path.

**Fix:** Added `refreshStretchBuffer()` call in `trimToLength()` with debug logging:
```cpp
refreshStretchBuffer();
StretchDebug::instance().logEarlyReturn(clipId, "trimToLength",
    "trim refreshed the stretched buffer for the new source range");
```

### Fix 3: Test Update — `tests/src/core/SampleStretchTest.cpp`

**Bug:** Test `trimWithStretchOffDoesNotTriggerProcessing()` asserted NO jobs after trim (pre-fix behavior).

**Fix:** Updated assertion to expect one additional job (post-fix behavior):
```cpp
// The fix causes a re-stretch request; one additional job must have completed.
QVERIFY(SampleStretchManager::instance().jobsCompleted() > jobsBeforeTrim);
```

